factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  reel_script says 'கம்யூனிஸ்ட் கட்சியினர்' (Communist party members) in the opening sentence; the article only names the Marxist Communist Party (மார்க்சிஸ்ட் கம்யூனிஸ்ட் கட்சி), which is consistent, but the reel_script's subsequent sentence names it again so no conflict — however the headline and slides frame the protest as 'Communist' generically, which is acceptable.
  reel_script states the protest was held 'at the Karur Corporation office' as the place of the demonstration, which matches the article; no problem there.
  reel_script adds that the 'ஜனநாயகபூர்வமான போராட்டங்களை' demand concerns the 'தீர்மானத்தை திரும்பப் பெற' — the article says the resolution forbidding such protests in front of taluk and collector offices should be withdrawn; the draft matches this, no problem.
  The slides_spec 'முக்கிய கோரிக்கை' slide states the old Amaravathi bridge is 'நூற்றாண்டு பழமையான' (centuries-old); the article says 'நூற்றாண்டு கண்ட கரூரின் அடையாளங்களில் ஒன்று' meaning one of Karur's landmarks that has seen a century, so 'நூற்றாண்டு பழமையான' is a slight reinterpretation, not a fabricated number.
  The slides_spec's 'பிற கோரிக்கைகள்' slide says the list of protest leaders includes 'மாவட்ட நிர்வாகி ஜோதிபாசு, சுப்பிரமணி உட்பட நிர்வாகிகள்' as a demand item, mixing a list of attendees into a list of demands, which is two different facts combined in one slide.
